<title>POLAND: KGHM copper output rises in 1st half.</title>
<headline>KGHM copper output rises in 1st half.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's KGHM Polska Miedz SA produced 218,680 tonnes of electrolytic copper in the first half of 1997, 3.5 percent more than in the same period of last year and 50.5 percent of the 1997 plan, KGHM said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement it also produced 511,763 kilograms of silver, which represented 50.8 percent of this year's plan and was 15.9 percent more than in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>--Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
